{
 "comment": "Server-side prompt caching, not a cache we control: the read-ahead pays for one prefill of what is new and the server serves the rest from its prefix cache. cut: where the stable prefix may end. word = the end of the last complete word, before the space (a cut after the space is not a token boundary: 'word ' tokenizes as [word, ' ▁'] but 'word more' as [word, ' ▁more'], and the prefix stops being a prefix). tokenize/logit_bias are per-server: with tokenize the engine counts tokens exactly and the META_BIAS of the frames comes back.",
